/**
 * Every creature's portrait: a kind of creature to each, drawn for ARISE on the 24-unit grid, after the reference games'
 * monster icons (docs/research/references/creature-icons/): a head or a bust, head-on wherever a face can be, filled
 * in one colour so it reads as a silhouette at 24 pixels, and its eyes a part of their own, lit. A creature shows it in
 * the colour it is set in, its eyes red; on red (a boss, its spotlight, a fight's card) red, its eyes white-hot; a Shadow
 * as the dark it became, rimmed in violet, its eyes violet (`Portrait`, `tone`). Its family's glyph (`ui/emblems.tsx`) stays the mark of its family, for Kin.
 *
 * The parts are path data, so the promotion's cinematic draws a Shadow's portrait on its canvas (`portraitPath`).
 */
